---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import profile from '../assets/brand/profile.png';
import { CATEGORIES } from '../data/categories';
import { CHANNEL, SERIES, seriesUrl } from '../data/series.mjs';
import { numberWord } from '../lib/words';
---

<Base title="About" description="VidyalAI publishes clear, sourced explainers on how large language models work, how they run fast, and how to build real systems with them.">
  <div class="container-narrow about">
    <header class="page-head about-head">
      <Image src={profile} alt="VidyalAI logo: an open book with glowing pixels rising from its pages." width={160} height={160} class="about-logo" />
      <div>
        <h1>About VidyalAI</h1>
        <p class="tagline">Knowledge amplified</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        VidyalAI is a learning resource for anyone curious about large language models, from first principles to
        production. The goal is simple: explain how things really work, clearly enough to act on and with sources
        you can check.
      </p>
      <p>The articles come in {numberWord(SERIES.length).toLowerCase()} series:</p>
      <ul>
        {SERIES.map((s) => <li><a href={seriesUrl(s.slug)}>{s.name}</a>: {s.blurb}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p>
        The <a href={seriesUrl('llm-system-design')}>LLM System Design</a> articles follow the same shape, so you
        can find what you need quickly:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>TL;DR:</strong> the answer in one paragraph.</li>
        <li><strong>Requirements to pin down first:</strong> the questions that change the design.</li>
        <li><strong>The design:</strong> components, numbers and worked examples.</li>
        <li><strong>How to measure it:</strong> metrics, targets and evals.</li>
        <li><strong>Tradeoffs</strong> and <strong>common mistakes</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Further reading:</strong> the papers and docs behind each claim.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Articles are also being turned into videos with the same diagrams and numbers, on the
        <a href={CHANNEL.url}>VidyalAI YouTube channel</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Topics</h2>
      <ul>
        {CATEGORIES.map((c) => <li><a href={`/category/${c.slug}/`}>{c.name}</a>: {c.blurb}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Numbers, prices and model names in this field go stale quickly. Each article cites its sources so you can check
        them. If you spot something wrong or out of date, please <a href="#contact">get in touch</a> so it can be fixed.
      </p>
      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, corrections or suggestions for a topic: email <strong>amit[at]vidyal.ai</strong> (replace
        <em>[at]</em> with <em>@</em>).
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .about-head h1 {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .about-logo {
    width: 120px;
    height: 120px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    box-shadow: 0 0 40px -10px var(--accent);
  }
  .tagline {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0 !important;
    font-size: 0.85rem !important;
    letter-spacing: 0.3em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent) !important;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
